course: dictionary
lesson: 7995
title: One word, many meanings: red
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings, and the words around it show you which one the writer means. Read the whole sentence before you decide. «The referee's word is final: a red card sends a player off.» Here red names a card, and the clue is that it sends a player off, so it is a sign, not a colour you see on a wall.
explain: Red can also describe a feeling or a money problem. «She went red when everyone clapped» tells you her face turned pink from shame or heat. «The shop is in the red this month» does not mean the shop is painted red. It means the shop owes money.
explain: Some phrases use red in a way that has nothing to do with colour. «See red» means to get very angry, and «paint the town red» means to go out and have fun. Ask yourself: does the sentence make sense if red means a colour? If not, it is probably a phrase, so think about what the whole phrase means.
fact: Red is the colour of strawberries, blood and fire trucks.
fact: To go red is to blush, when your face turns pink from shame or heat.
fact: «In the red» means owing money, having less than nothing in the bank.
fact: «See red» means to get very angry, and a «red-letter day» is a very special day.
fact: Scarlet and crimson are shades of red, often used in science and exams.
exercise: In «cooler stars are orange or red», what does red mean? | A very special day | A feeling of shame | Owing money | *A colour
exercise: «The referee's word is final: a red card sends a player off.» What does a red card do? | It marks a wrong answer in class | It is only a warning | It means the team has won | *It sends a player off
exercise: «The shop is in the red this month.» What does in the red mean? | It is a very special day | It is painted red | It is very angry | *It owes money
test: «Lily went red when the whole class sang to her.» What does went red mean here? | She ran out of the room | *She blushed, and her face turned pink | She turned into a red fire truck | She was very angry with the class
test: Which word is a shade of red? | Owing | *Scarlet | Blush | Deficit
exam: In «a deficit», the word means owing money. Which phrase in ordinary talk means the same? | Red-letter day | *In the red | Paint the town red | See red
